  "findings": [
    "All45 frozen comment macros exist in the preceding account and match the actual source. Independent lexical audit checks complete templates and every non-comment argument, including five mixed element macros. No comment removed; all other tokens unchanged except one function-signature formatting comma. Exactly nine production files; no sequence, geometry, parser/model, comparator or baseline changes.",
    "OpenJDK21.0.5 ToStream.comment dash insertion/padding matches the shared helper. Literal ASCII &, <, > and quotes are retained by source. Lowercase us-ascii selects Encodings.getWriter/StreamEncoder REPLACE. US_ASCII.Encoder returns Surrogate.Parser.unmappableResult: one error of length2 for a valid surrogate pair; Charset-X-Coder emits the replacement once then advances by that length. Fresh X\ud834\udd1eY and X\u00e9Y both produce X?Y, including reverse link comments: one ?, not two.",
    "Fresh whole comment cohort: 4\u21928/22 valid, 30 total with eight nonpositive Java references. Four valid inputs class \"--\", class \"----\", class \"-->\", class \"<!--\" panic before and after at parser parse/class.rs:285, indexing parts[0] with an empty identity path. These remain executable counterexamples; no claim the comment helper caused the pre-existing panic.",
    "Cluster Shelf<!--]]>-- emits Java cluster Shelf<!- -]]>- - but Rust cluster Shelf..- -...- -. Deployment/description Unicode link endpoints retain identifier normalization/selection differences despite matching entity comment lists. Object/legacy activity outputs omit expected comments along with their missing/wrong whole diagram. Unicode metrics/layout still diverge. These are consumer/dataflow failures, not serializer escapes to tune.",
    "The initial eight unicode_* probes all disagree with intended validity: five Java SAXException crash SVGs and three syntax errors. They contain no literal C0 source bytes. Source-proven cause of manufactured NUL: literal U+E000 reaches AtomText constructor:80 \u2192 CharHidder.unhide \u2192 unhideChar:87\u201388, which subtracts U+E000 from the reserved U+E000..E0FF range. Stack confirms ToStream.accumDefaultEscape:1749 throws for U+0000. Eight safe follow-up references are valid diagrams and cover the requested consumers, BMP categories, NBSP/combining marks, and four supplementary characters; none pass whole-output comparison.",
    "Across54 fresh cases there are four existing panics and seven remaining malformed outputs (all in initial invalid-reference Unicode cases), with zero new errors/panics/lost passes. Fresh malformed count falls17\u21927. Category Cs cannot be a UTF-8 Unicode scalar; private/unassigned/separator category probes remain nonpositive, not invented positive coverage."
  ],
